# G5/G5.1 vectors. Numbers in [] are catalog IDs from ../../README.md.
# Every test starts at machine X-100 Y-100 Z-10; most set work zero there.

# ---- basics ----------------------------------------------------------------

= basic S
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G17 G21 G90 G94 F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
pos -90 -100 -10

= [7] negative P, the usual CAM S-curve @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P-3 Q3
pos -90 -100 -10

= [6] G5 without X/Y does not move to machine zero @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 I1 J1 P1 Q1 -> any
pos -100 -100 -10

= [6] G5.1 without X/Y does not move to machine zero @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5.1 I1 J1 -> any
pos -100 -100 -10

# ---- accuracy [1] [2] [3] [24] ---------------------------------------------

# Inflection on the midpoint of t in [0, 0.1] (t = 0.05): the chord of that
# interval runs along X and the curve adds A*(s^3 - 1.5s^2 + 0.5s) in Y, which
# is zero at the midpoint, so a midpoint probe sees no deviation where there
# is 0.0481*A mm, here A = 10.
= [1] inflection on a probed midpoint does not hide the deviation
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y8550 I-3.3333 J16.6667 P3.3333 Q-9016.667

= [2] long handles 1e3
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I1000 J1000 P1000 Q1000

= [2] long handles 1e4
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I10000 J10000 P10000 Q10000

= [2] long handles 1e5
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I100000 J100000 P100000 Q100000

# About 1700 segments: within the tolerance and under the cap of 2000.
= [2] handles 1e5 with opposite Q stay within the tolerance
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X100000 Y0 I1 J1 P100000 Q-100000

# Past BEZIER_MAX_SEGMENTS (2000, the default maxseg) the tolerance is given
# up: absurd handles get the cap, never an endless or undefined count.
= [2] handles 1e7: capped at 2000 segments, deviation 1.6 mm
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
set tol 2
G5 X10 Y0 I10000000 J10000000 P10000000 Q10000000

= [2] long curve 1 m
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X1000 Y0 I300 J300 P300 Q300

# Built with BEZIER_SIGMA=settings.arc_tolerance the deviation is checked
# against $12 as it stands. 11 segments is what 0.1 mm takes for this curve,
# so maxseg shows that a coarser $12 is followed too.
= [56] $12 is the tolerance of G5: default, coarse and fine @tol
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
set arctol 0.1
set maxseg 11
G5 X20 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
set arctol 0.0001
set maxseg 2000
G5 X30 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3

# 0.8/$12 is infinite, and not a number once multiplied by a zero bend: both
# end at the cap.
= [56] $12 = 0: the cap of 2000 segments, nothing divided by zero @tol
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
set arctol 0
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
G5.1 X20 Y0 I5 J5
G5 X30 Y0 I0 J0 P0 Q0
G5 X30 Y0 I0 J0 P0 Q0

= [3] basic S rotated by 45 degrees
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X7.071068 Y7.071068 I0 J4.242641 P0 Q4.242641

= [24] tiny curve below step resolution
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0.002 Y0 I0.001 J0.001 P0.001 Q0.001

= [24] near-zero handles
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0.000001 Y0 I0.000001 J0.000001 P0.000001 Q0.000001

= [24] all control points coincident
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0 Y0 I0 J0 P0 Q0 -> any

= far from origin, 60000 mm
F1000
G53 G0 X-60000 Y-60000
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3

= closed loop, start == end
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0 Y0 I10 J0 P0 Q10

# ---- non-finite and overflowing values [5] [42] ----------------------------

= [42] 40-digit literal is rejected, not read as inf @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I1000000000000000000000000000000000000000 J0 P1 Q1 -> error

= [5] handles near float overflow: no garbage targets (same class as G1 X1e35) @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
set tol 0.1
G5 X10 Y0 I100000000000000000000000000000000000 J0 P1 Q1 -> any

# ---- geometry equivalences [12] [13] [14] [15] [16] [17] [18] [31] [36] -----

= [12] cusp: the planner stops at the reversal
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y0 I-10 J10 P10 Q10
junction 50

= [13] smooth chain with implicit I/J has no corner at the join
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
set smooth 1
G5 X-10 Y0 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
G5 X-20 Y0 P3 Q-3
X-30 Y0 P3 Q3
pos -130 -100 -10

= [14] handles on the chord: same as G1
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
set tol 0.0001
G5 X-30 Y0 I-10 J0 P10 Q0
G5 X-60 Y-15 I-10 J-5 P10 Q5

= [14] straight with overshooting handles
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X30 Y0 I40 J0 P40 Q0

= [15] G5.1 equals G5 with 2/3-rule handles
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5.1 X-20 Y0 I-10 J10
G0 X0 Y0
G5 X-20 Y0 I-6.6666667 J6.6666667 P6.6666667 Q6.6666667
same 0 0 0

= [16] quarter circle R10 within the Bezier-circle error
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y10 I0 J5.5228475 P5.5228475 Q0
circle -110 -100 10 0.003

= [17] translation by G91
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y0 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
G91 G5 X-10 Y0 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
same -10 0 0

= [17] translation by G92
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y0 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
G92 X0 Y0
G5 X-10 Y0 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
same -10 0 0

= [17] G20 equals G21
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y0 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
G20 G91 G5 X-0.39370079 Y0 I-0.11811024 J0.11811024 P0.11811024 Q0.11811024 F39.370079
same -10 0 0

= [18] curve and its reverse
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y0 I2 J5 P2 Q5
G5 X0 Y0 I2 J5 P2 Q5
pos -100 -100 -10

= [31] same line from the same point gives the same segments
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y0 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
G0 X0 Y0
G5 X-10 Y0 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
same 0 0 0

= [36] soft reset, then the same line gives the same segments
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y0 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
G0 X0 Y0
reset
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y0 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
same 0 0 0

# ---- modes and state [8] [19] [29] [30] [38] [39] -------------------------

= [38] first G5 needs I and J
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 P3 Q3 -> error

= [38] P and Q are required
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 -> error
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 Q0 -> error

= [38] continuation with only I: J is 0
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 Q5
G5 X20 Y0 I1 P0 Q5
pos -80 -100 -10

= [30] modal continuation with P/Q and implicit I/J
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 Q5
X20 Y0 P0 Q5
pos -80 -100 -10

= [30] modal continuation without P/Q
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 Q5
X20 Y0 -> error

= [8] rejected block does not change implicit I/J @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 Q5
G5 X20 Y0 P0 Q7 R1 -> error
G5 X20 Y0 P0 Q5

= [8] rejected jog does not change implicit I/J @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 Q5
$J=G5X20Y0I1J1P0Q7F100 -> error
G5 X20 Y0 P0 Q5

= [19] G5 after G5.1 needs I/J
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5.1 X10 Y0 I5 J5
G5 X20 Y0 P0 Q5 -> error

= [19] G5 after G1 needs I/J
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 Q5
G1 X12
G5 X20 Y0 P0 Q5 -> error

= [19] check mode parses without motion
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
set check 1
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
pos -90 -100 -10

= [38] G5.1 needs I and J, not both zero
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5.1 X10 Y0 I5 -> error
G5.1 X10 Y0 I0 J0 -> error

= no feed rate
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error:22

= [29] G93 without F on the block
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error

= [39] G93 G5 takes 1/F minutes @bug @!g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 F2

= [39] G93 G5.1 takes 1/F minutes @bug @!g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5.1 X10 Y0 I5 J5 F2

# The arcs of upstream Grbl for comparison: mc_arc multiplies F by the segment
# count and clears the inverse time flag, so the arc runs at F*segments mm/min.
# The half circle of radius 5 has 55 segments at $12 = 0.002 and takes 0.071 min.
= [55] G93 G1 takes 1/F minutes
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G1 X20 Y0 F2
minutes 0.4999 0.5001

= [55] G93 G2 takes 1/F minutes @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G2 X10 Y0 I5 J0 F4
minutes 0.2499 0.2501

# ---- spelling and forbidden combinations [25] [26] [27] [41] -----------------

= [25] command spelling
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G05 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
G5.0 X20 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
G5.10 X30 Y0 I3 J3
G5.01 X40 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error
G5.2 X40 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error
pos -70 -100 -10

= [26] number spelling
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P.5 Q3
G5 X20 Y0 I3 J3 P+5 Q3
G5 X30 Y0 I3 J3 P5. Q3
G5 X40 Y0 I3 J3 P1E3 Q3 -> error
G5 X40 Y0 I3 J3 P Q3 -> error
pos -70 -100 -10

= [26] number spelling, negative fraction @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P-.5 Q3
pos -90 -100 -10

= [27] forbidden combinations
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G53 G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error
G5 G1 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error
G18 G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error
G19 G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error
G18 G5.1 X10 Y0 I3 J3 -> error
G28 G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error
pos -100 -100 -10

= [27] Z word without BEZIER_Z_LINEAR @!z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z-1 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error
G5.1 X10 Y0 Z-1 I5 J5 -> error
pos -100 -100 -10

# The preceding G5 has the same P/Q, so the known spline_pq write [8] leaves
# the state unchanged and the status check stays strict (no @bug masking).
= [27] unused words R, K, L
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
G5 X20 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 R1 -> error
G5 X20 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 K1 -> error
G5 X20 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 L1 -> error
pos -90 -100 -10

# ---- machine and environment [32] [33] [40] --------------------------------

= [32] 1 step per mm: segments shorter than a step
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
set steps 1
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
G5 X10.3 Y0.2 I0.1 J0.1 P0.1 Q0.1

= [32] 1000 steps per mm, slow axes
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
set steps 1000
set rate 100
set accel 1
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3

= [33] tool length offset
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G43.1 Z5
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
pos -90 -100 -10

= [40] soft limits: curve leaves the envelope between inside endpoints @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
set soft 1
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J150 P0 Q150 -> error
